{
  "id": "017",
  "title": "The Inheritance Clause",
  "subtitle": "\"I had forty-three days to find a husband. I called the only man I had ever trusted: the boy who'd been my best friend until the summer we both turned twenty-one.\"",
  "penName": "Meredith Drake",
  "genre": "contractMarriage",
  "hook": "My grandfather left me a New York brownstone, fourteen million dollars, and a clause: married before my twenty-eighth birthday or it all goes to the Metropolitan Opera. I had forty-three days. I called Theodore Wren. We had been each other's best friends from nine to twenty-one. The last time I saw him he was getting on a train to Oxford and I was pretending I did not love him. I flew to London. He opened his door. He said, \"Say the whole sentence.\" I said, \"Marry me, Theo, for a year.\" He said, \"Yes, Meredith. Of course.\"",
